  "body": "## What changed\nFace-normal alignment picks no longer trust facet winding blindly. Before, an inside-out mesh made \"lay this face on G17\" turn the part upside down, and made a 3-2-1 pick the opposite side, silently.\n\n**New `crates/app/src/pick/winding.rs`** gives each body a verdict.\n- A body is a set of facets connected through shared edges. Vertices within 1e-4 mm count as the same point.\n- Edges are counted by direction, which sorts a body into **Open**, **NonManifold** or **Mixed** winding.\n- The signed volume (divergence theorem; Zhang & Chen 2001) gives **Outward**, **InsideOut** or **Flat**.\n- Verdicts are cached for the last 8 meshes (thread-local), keyed by a hash of the facets that depends on winding.\n\n**`pick/align.rs` `outward_normal`** refuses, by name, any face whose body is not Outward. The face lay, the two-edge lay and the 3-2-1 all go through it. Example message: `face … of 'cube_inside_out' belongs to a body whose facets are inside-out (wound inward), so its outside would be read backwards - fix the model's facet winding (re-export it) before aligning to it`.\n\n**The design is to refuse at pick time; nothing is repaired at import.** User geometry, existing toolpaths and the goldens are unchanged. Alternatives are in `docs/decisions/366-inverted-winding.md`.\n\n**Behaviour change users will notice:** face-normal picks on an **open or non-manifold** mesh, which used to be accepted, now refuse by name. That is what the issue asks for. The existing Repair mesh button is the way out.\n\n## Readings\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test winding_align`: 9/9 pass.\n- These existing suites pass: plane_align, plane_align_edges, wcs_align, setup_align, vertex_pick, face_origin, pick and repair_model.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick upstream/main` (after merging upstream/main): every app suite passes.\n- camcraft-ui suites: only the known GPU headless reds (`headless_run_succeeds`, `headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`, `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`).\n- All five shipped testdata models read Outward.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/winding_align.rs`)\n- An inverted cube refuses the face lay and the plane-side readout, the two-edge lay and the 3-2-1.\n- The same cube wound outward still aligns.\n- An open box refuses all three picks.\n- Mixed-winding and non-manifold bodies refuse.\n- In a two-body mesh, the good body lays and the bad one refuses.\n- The shipped models read Outward.\n- The fixture `testdata/models/cube_inside_out.stl` refuses.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No GUI hand test yet; a test binary has been built.\n- Large-mesh performance was not measured. The check runs per pick and per frame for the plane-side readout. It is cached, but the content hash is computed each time, at about the cost of the existing feature digest.\n- A face that spans two bodies has its logic reviewed but no test.\n\nChangelog: Alignment picks (face lay, two-edge lay, 3-2-1) refuse by name on a body whose facets are inside-out, open or non-manifold, instead of silently flipping the part (#366)\n\nFixes #366\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
